<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $16.7 mln Oct 17.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $16.7 mln Oct 17.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $16.7 million deficit on October 17 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON OCTOBER 17</p>
<p>Exports: $146.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $174.5 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $201.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $190.3 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $16.7 million</p>
<p>OCTOBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.155 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.172 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.652 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.112 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.523 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
